{
  "schemaVersion": "explainer-kit.author-result/v2",
  "artifactId": "project-recap",
  "content": {
    "html": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n    <title>Wave 2: making sync version skew visible</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"One defect, one lane: oat sync quietly restamped a stale manifest version during apply, erasing the producer and invoker mismatch that is the first suspect in stale-tooling incidents.\" />\n    <style>\n      :root {\n        --canvas: #f4f6f9;\n          --panel: #ffffff;\n          --elevated: #eef1f5;\n          --border: color-mix(in srgb, #4a5568 26%, transparent);\n          --ink: #16202e;\n          --muted: #4a5568;\n          --accent: #2f56c9;\n          --accent-2: #0e7180;\n          --success: #157a54;\n          --warning: #965108;\n          --danger: #bd3a2c;\n        --sans: system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, sans-serif;\n        --serif: ui-serif, Georgia, serif;\n        --mono: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Consolas, monospace;\n        --radius: 8px;\n        --radius-lg: 12px;\n        --rule: 1px solid var(--border);\n        --measure: 66ch;\n      }\n      @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {\n        :root {\n          --canvas: #111827;\n          --panel: #1f2937;\n          --elevated: #374151;\n          --border: color-mix(in srgb, #d1d5db 26%, transparent);\n          --ink: #f9fafb;\n          --muted: #d1d5db;\n          --accent: #93c5fd;\n          --accent-2: #5eead4;\n          --success: #86efac;\n          --warning: #fde047;\n          --danger: #fca5a5;\n        }\n      }\n      * { box-sizing: border-box; }\n      html {\n        color-scheme: light dark;\n        scroll-behavior: smooth;\n      }\n      body {\n        margin: 0;\n        background: var(--canvas);\n        color: var(--ink);\n        font-family: var(--sans);\n        font-size: 1rem;\n        line-height: 1.65;\n        -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%;\n      }\n      a { color: var(--accent); }\n      a:focus-visible,\n      .toc a:focus-visible {\n        outline: 2px solid var(--accent);\n        outline-offset: 2px;\n      }\n      .wrap {\n        display: grid;\n        grid-template-columns: minmax(11rem, 15rem) minmax(0, 1fr);\n        gap: 2.5rem;\n        max-width: 76rem;\n        margin: 0 auto;\n        padding: 2.5rem 2rem 4rem;\n      }\n      main { min-width: 0; }\n\n      /* Typographic roles */\n      .eyebrow,\n      .toc-label,\n      .label {\n        font: 700 0.68rem/1.4 var(--mono);\n        letter-spacing: 0.14em;\n        text-transform: uppercase;\n        color: var(--muted);\n      }\n      h1 {\n        font-family: var(--serif);\n        font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 6vw, 3.4rem);\n        font-weight: 600;\n        line-height: 1.08;\n        letter-spacing: -0.015em;\n        margin: 0.6rem 0 0;\n        text-wrap: balance;\n      }\n      .lede {\n        font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 2.4vw, 1.3rem);\n        line-height: 1.5;\n        max-width: 46ch;\n        margin: 1rem 0 0;\n        color: var(--ink);\n      }\n      h2 {\n        font-family: var(--serif);\n        font-size: clamp(1.45rem, 3.2vw, 1.9rem);\n        font-weight: 600;\n        line-height: 1.15;\n        margin: 0 0 1.1rem;\n        padding-bottom: 0.5rem;\n        border-bottom: var(--rule);\n        scroll-margin-top: 1.5rem;\n        text-wrap: balance;\n      }\n      h3 {\n        font-family: var(--sans);\n        font-size: 1.05rem;\n        font-weight: 650;\n        line-height: 1.3;\n        margin: 0 0 0.4rem;\n      }\n      p { margin: 0 0 1rem; max-width: var(--measure); }\n      .note {\n        font-size: 0.875rem;\n        line-height: 1.5;\n        color: var(--muted);\n      }\n      code, pre { font-family: var(--mono); }\n      :not(pre) > code {\n        font-size: 0.86em;\n        background: var(--elevated);\n        border-radius: 4px;\n        padding: 0.08em 0.32em;\n        overflow-wrap: anywhere;\n      }\n\n      /* Navigation rail */\n      .toc {\n        position: sticky;\n        top: 2rem;\n        align-self: start;\n        max-height: calc(100dvh - 4rem);\n        overflow-y: auto;\n      }\n      .toc-label { display: block; margin-bottom: 0.8rem; }\n      .toc ol {\n        list-style: none;\n        margin: 0;\n        padding: 0;\n        counter-reset: toc;\n      }\n      .toc a {\n        display: block;\n        border-left: 2px solid var(--border);\n        padding: 0.32rem 0 0.32rem 0.75rem;\n        color: var(--muted);\n        font-size: 0.9rem;\n        line-height: 1.35;\n        text-decoration: none;\n      }\n      .toc a:hover { color: var(--ink); }\n      .toc a.active {\n        border-left-color: var(--accent);\n        color: var(--ink);\n        font-weight: 650;\n      }\n\n      /* Masthead and status */\n      .masthead { margin-bottom: 3rem; }\n      .status-strip {\n        display: grid;\n        grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 9.5rem), 1fr));\n        gap: 1px;\n        background: var(--border);\n        border: var(--rule);\n        border-radius: var(--radius-lg);\n        overflow: hidden;\n        margin-top: 2rem;\n      }\n      .stat {\n        background: var(--panel);\n        padding: 0.95rem 1.1rem;\n      }\n      .stat .label { display: block; }\n      .stat b {\n        display: block;\n        font-family: var(--serif);\n        font-size: 1.45rem;\n        font-weight: 600;\n        line-height: 1.15;\n        margin-top: 0.25rem;\n      }\n      .stat.is-good b { color: var(--success); }\n      .stat.is-open b { color: var(--warning); }\n      .stat span.sub {\n        display: block;\n        font-size: 0.8rem;\n        color: var(--muted);\n      }\n\n      section { margin-bottom: 3.5rem; }\n\n      /* Section 1: the before and after, then the accepted contract */\n      .before-after {\n        display: grid;\n        grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 18rem), 1fr));\n        gap: 1px;\n        background: var(--border);\n        border: var(--rule);\n        border-radius: var(--radius-lg);\n        overflow: hidden;\n        margin: 1.6rem 0 0;\n      }\n      .before-after > div {\n        background: var(--panel);\n        padding: 1.1rem 1.2rem;\n        min-width: 0;\n      }\n      .before-after .label { display: block; margin-bottom: 0.35rem; }\n      .before-after p { margin: 0; max-width: none; }\n      .before-after .is-before .label { color: var(--danger); }\n      .before-after .is-after .label { color: var(--success); }\n      .contract {\n        list-style: none;\n        margin: 1.5rem 0 0;\n        padding: 0;\n        display: grid;\n        gap: 0.65rem;\n        max-width: var(--measure);\n        counter-reset: rule;\n      }\n      .contract li {\n        display: grid;\n        grid-template-columns: 1.6rem 1fr;\n        gap: 0.6rem;\n        align-items: baseline;\n      }\n      .contract li::before {\n        content: counter(rule);\n        counter-increment: rule;\n        font: 700 0.7rem/1.6 var(--mono);\n        color: var(--accent);\n      }\n\n      /* Section 2: decisions */\n      .decisions {\n        list-style: none;\n        margin: 0;\n        padding: 0;\n        counter-reset: decision;\n        display: grid;\n        gap: 1.6rem;\n      }\n      .decisions > li {\n        display: grid;\n        grid-template-columns: 2.6rem minmax(0, 1fr);\n        gap: 0.4rem 1rem;\n        padding-top: 1.2rem;\n        border-top: var(--rule);\n      }\n      .decisions > li::before {\n        content: counter(decision, decimal-leading-zero);\n        counter-increment: decision;\n        font: 600 1.4rem/1 var(--serif);\n        color: var(--accent);\n      }\n      .decisions h3 { grid-column: 2; }\n      .decisions dl {\n        grid-column: 2;\n        margin: 0.5rem 0 0;\n        display: grid;\n        grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);\n        gap: 0.5rem 1.2rem;\n        max-width: var(--measure);\n      }\n      .decisions dt {\n        font: 700 0.68rem/1.4 var(--mono);\n        letter-spacing: 0.14em;\n        text-transform: uppercase;\n        color: var(--muted);\n      }\n      .decisions dd { margin: 0.1rem 0 0; }\n      @media (min-width: 52rem) {\n        .decisions dl { grid-template-columns: 5.5rem minmax(0, 1fr); }\n        .decisions dt { text-align: right; padding-top: 0.28rem; }\n        .decisions dd { margin-top: 0; }\n      }\n\n      /* Section 3: architecture */\n      figure { margin: 1.5rem 0 0; }\n      .diagram-scroll {\n        max-width: 100%;\n        overflow-x: auto;\n        border: var(--rule);\n        border-radius: var(--radius-lg);\n        background: var(--canvas);\n        padding: 1rem;\n      }\n      svg.diagram {\n        display: block;\n        width: 100%;\n        min-width: 40rem;\n        height: auto;\n      }\n      .diagram .node { fill: var(--panel); stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1; }\n      .diagram .node.is-lane { fill: var(--elevated); stroke: var(--accent); }\n      .diagram .node.is-blocked { fill: var(--panel); stroke: var(--warning); stroke-dasharray: 5 4; }\n      .diagram .node.is-goal { fill: var(--panel); stroke: var(--success); stroke-width: 2; }\n      .diagram .edge { fill: none; stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 2; }\n      .diagram .edge.is-feedback { stroke: var(--muted); stroke-dasharray: 6 5; }\n      .diagram .arrow { fill: var(--accent); }\n      .diagram .arrow.is-muted { fill: var(--muted); }\n      .diagram .node-label {\n        fill: var(--ink);\n        font: 650 14px var(--sans);\n      }\n      .diagram .node-sub {\n        fill: var(--muted);\n        font: 11px var(--mono);\n      }\n      .diagram .edge-label {\n        fill: var(--muted);\n        font: 11px var(--mono);\n      }\n      figcaption {\n        margin-top: 0.75rem;\n        font-size: 0.875rem;\n        color: var(--muted);\n        max-width: var(--measure);\n      }\n      .lanes {\n        display: grid;\n        grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 17rem), 1fr));\n        gap: 1.25rem;\n        margin-top: 2rem;\n      }\n      .lane {\n        min-width: 0;\n        border-top: 3px solid var(--accent);\n        padding-top: 0.9rem;\n      }\n      .lane.is-secondary { border-top-color: var(--muted); }\n      .lane ul { margin: 0.6rem 0 0; padding-left: 1.1rem; }\n      .lane li { margin-bottom: 0.35rem; }\n\n      /* Tables */\n      .table-scroll {\n        max-width: 100%;\n        overflow-x: auto;\n        margin-top: 1.4rem;\n      }\n      table {\n        width: 100%;\n        min-width: 38rem;\n        border-collapse: collapse;\n        font-size: 0.94rem;\n      }\n      caption {\n        text-align: left;\n        font: 700 0.68rem/1.4 var(--mono);\n        letter-spacing: 0.14em;\n        text-transform: uppercase;\n        color: var(--muted);\n        padding-bottom: 0.6rem;\n      }\n      th, td {\n        border-bottom: var(--rule);\n        padding: 0.62rem 0.9rem 0.62rem 0;\n        text-align: left;\n        vertical-align: top;\n      }\n      thead th {\n        font: 700 0.68rem/1.4 var(--mono);\n        letter-spacing: 0.12em;\n        text-transform: uppercase;\n        color: var(--muted);\n        border-bottom-width: 2px;\n      }\n      tbody th { font-weight: 650; white-space: nowrap; }\n      td.evidence { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--muted); }\n      td.ok { color: var(--success); }\n\n      /* Section 6: outcome */\n      .outcome {\n        display: grid;\n        gap: 1.75rem;\n        margin-top: 0.5rem;\n      }\n      .outcome > div { max-width: var(--measure); }\n      .outcome h3 { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 0.55rem; }\n      .outcome h3 .label { letter-spacing: 0.14em; }\n      .outcome ul { margin: 0.5rem 0 0; padding-left: 1.15rem; }\n      .outcome li { margin-bottom: 0.45rem; }\n      .outcome .works { border-left: 3px solid var(--success); padding-left: 1rem; }\n      .outcome .gaps { border-left: 3px solid var(--warning); padding-left: 1rem; }\n      .outcome .next { border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); padding-left: 1rem; }\n\n      footer {\n        margin-top: 3.5rem;\n        padding-top: 1.2rem;\n        border-top: var(--rule);\n        color: var(--muted);\n        font-size: 0.85rem;\n      }\n      footer p { max-width: var(--measure); }\n\n      @media (max-width: 52rem) {\n        .wrap {\n          grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);\n          gap: 1.25rem;\n          padding: 1rem 1rem 3rem;\n        }\n        .toc {\n          position: sticky;\n          top: 0;\n          z-index: 2;\n          max-height: none;\n          overflow-x: auto;\n          overflow-y: hidden;\n          background: var(--canvas);\n          border-bottom: var(--rule);\n          padding: 0.6rem 0;\n          margin: 0 -1rem;\n          padding-left: 1rem;\n          padding-right: 1rem;\n        }\n        .toc-label { display: none; }\n        .toc ol { display: flex; gap: 0.3rem; }\n        .toc a {\n          flex: none;\n          white-space: nowrap;\n          border-left: 0;\n          border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);\n          padding: 0.2rem 0.55rem;\n          font-size: 0.82rem;\n        }\n        .toc a.active { border-bottom-color: var(--accent); border-left-color: transparent; }\n        .decisions > li { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }\n        .decisions > li::before { grid-column: 1; }\n        .decisions h3, .decisions dl { grid-column: 1; }\n      }\n      @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {\n        html { scroll-behavior: auto; }\n      }\n    </style>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div class=\"wrap\">\n      <nav class=\"toc\" aria-label=\"Recap sections\">\n        <span class=\"toc-label\">OAT project recap / shared / wave-2-execution</span>\n        <ol>\n          <li><a href=\"#original-request\">What was asked for</a></li>\n          <li><a href=\"#key-agent-decisions\">Decisions that shaped the result</a></li>\n          <li><a href=\"#as-built-architecture\">How the wave was built</a></li>\n          <li><a href=\"#implementation-record\">What changed</a></li>\n          <li><a href=\"#validation-evidence\">How it was checked</a></li>\n          <li><a href=\"#outcome\">Where this leaves the repository</a></li>\n        </ol>\n      </nav>\n      <main>\n        <header class=\"masthead\">\n          <span class=\"eyebrow\">OAT project recap / shared / wave-2-execution</span>\n          <h1>Wave 2: making sync version skew visible</h1>\n          <p class=\"lede\">A sync manifest remembers which CLI wrote it. Apply used to overwrite that memory before anyone could read it, so a mismatched toolchain looked identical to a healthy one.</p>\n          <div class=\"status-strip\">\n            <div class=\"stat is-good\">\n              <span class=\"label\">Implementation</span>\n              <b>Complete</b>\n              <span class=\"sub\">1 of 1 lanes, both review rounds closed</span>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"stat is-good\">\n              <span class=\"label\">Definition of done</span>\n              <b>Green</b>\n              <span class=\"sub\">8 gates, every exit code 0</span>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"stat is-good\">\n              <span class=\"label\">Reviews</span>\n              <b>Passed</b>\n              <span class=\"sub\">plan gate, phase, final and exit gate</span>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"stat is-open\">\n              <span class=\"label\">Remaining</span>\n              <b>Wave PR</b>\n              <span class=\"sub\">not yet opened or merged</span>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </header>\n        <section id=\"original-request\" aria-labelledby=\"original-request-heading\">\n          <h2 id=\"original-request-heading\">What was asked for</h2>\n          <p>Wave 2 of the 2026-08-19 execution program carried a single small defect, so the wrapper OAT project has exactly one lane. <code>oat sync</code> loads a sync manifest that records the CLI version that produced it, and apply restamps that field to the invoking version. The restamp happened silently, which meant the one signal that a different toolchain had last written the manifest was destroyed on the way past.</p>\n          <div class=\"before-after\">\n            <div class=\"is-before\">\n              <span class=\"label\">Before</span>\n              <p>A manifest written by an older or newer CLI was restamped during apply with no output at all. Nothing in human or JSON mode distinguished it from a manifest the current CLI had written itself.</p>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"is-after\">\n              <span class=\"label\">After</span>\n              <p>Each scope carries a <code>versionSkew</code> diagnostic. Human mode warns once per skewed scope before the restamp; JSON mode carries the same structured array and stays byte-clean on stderr.</p>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n          <p>The request was deliberately narrow. Version skew stays advisory: it changes no exit code, no planned-operation count, no apply eligibility and no manifest schema. That narrowness is what let a one-task lane close a defect that had already misled earlier stale-tooling investigations.</p>\n          <h3>The constraints the wrapper accepted</h3>\n          <ol class=\"contract\">\n            <li>The lane's entire implementation contract is its immutable external plan. The wrapper adds ordering, gates, review mapping and bookkeeping, and restates none of it.</li>\n            <li>Run the source plan's drift check in the worktree before editing, extended by the plan gate to the release surfaces the plan itself writes.</li>\n            <li>Honour every source-plan STOP condition verbatim; a tripped STOP parks the lane instead of weakening the plan.</li>\n            <li>Confirm the source plan's own done criteria, then run the full definition of done, invoking each gate literally and capturing every exit code to a log.</li>\n            <li>Keep reviewed history append-only: fix rounds land as new commits and no reviewed SHA is amended.</li>\n          </ol>\n          <p class=\"note\">Success meant the source plan's done criteria confirmed and recorded, every review row <code>passed</code>, and the full definition of done green on the wave branch.</p>\n        </section>\n        <section id=\"key-agent-decisions\" aria-labelledby=\"key-agent-decisions-heading\">\n          <h2 id=\"key-agent-decisions-heading\">Decisions that shaped the result</h2>\n          <p>Four choices changed what shipped or how it got there. Each is recorded with the reason it was made and the consequence it carried.</p>\n          <ol class=\"decisions\">\n            <li>\n              <h3>Derive the apply restamp from the skew diagnostic</h3>\n              <dl>\n                <dt>Reason</dt>\n                <dd>The first review round found the same \"does the recorded version differ\" test written twice: once to build the diagnostic and once to decide whether apply should restamp. Nothing held the two copies in agreement.</dd>\n                <dt>Consequence</dt>\n                <dd>Apply now keys off the diagnostic the warning is built from, so the advisory and the restamp cannot drift apart. Two unreachable empty-string guards were removed to make the derivation bit-for-bit the old predicate, and a desync mutation is now caught by a dedicated coupling test.</dd>\n              </dl>\n            </li>\n            <li>\n              <h3>Pre-plan the lockstep bump as part of the lane</h3>\n              <dl>\n                <dt>Reason</dt>\n                <dd>Wave 1 discovered at fan-in that any change under the CLI source tree, tests included, counts as a publishable change. Here the same rule was applied while planning instead.</dd>\n                <dt>Consequence</dt>\n                <dd>The drift refresh intersected the write surface with the release change-detection roots and stated the 0.2.33 to 0.2.34 bump up front, so the lane carried it rather than the root patching it afterwards.</dd>\n              </dl>\n            </li>\n            <li>\n              <h3>Extend the in-worktree drift check beyond the source plan</h3>\n              <dl>\n                <dt>Reason</dt>\n                <dd>The source plan's drift command omitted two surfaces its own implementation depends on or writes: the shared version constant, and the five public package manifests against a freshly fetched baseline.</dd>\n                <dt>Consequence</dt>\n                <dd>The plan gate added both as a wrapper-level addendum, with a fetch before every release gate run. An advance of the public-package baseline after planning became a STOP rather than a bump from a stale number.</dd>\n              </dl>\n            </li>\n            <li>\n              <h3>Treat the blocked exit gate as an operator boundary</h3>\n              <dl>\n                <dt>Reason</dt>\n                <dd>The configured cross-family exit gate blocked twice: its headless child pushed the gate commands onto background work and ended its turn without writing an artifact.</dd>\n                <dt>Consequence</dt>\n                <dd>Autonomy stopped at the configured attempt cap rather than retrying around it. The operator changed the target selection, and a second generation ran the whole definition of done in the foreground and passed.</dd>\n              </dl>\n            </li>\n        </ol>\n        </section>\n        <section id=\"as-built-architecture\" aria-labelledby=\"as-built-architecture-heading\">\n          <h2 id=\"as-built-architecture-heading\">How the wave was built</h2>\n          <p>With one lane there is no fan-out to manage, so the interesting structure is vertical: the loops that a change had to survive before it counted as done. Two of them fired, and both are visible in the record.</p>\n          <figure>\n            <div class=\"diagram-scroll\">\n              <svg class=\"diagram\" viewBox=\"0 0 900 712\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"arch-title arch-desc\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMin meet\">\n                <title id=\"arch-title\">Wave 2 execution architecture</title>\n                <desc id=\"arch-desc\">The 2026-08-19 execution program scopes the wave-2-execution wrapper project. The wrapper plan goes through a configured artifact gate that blocked it twice before passing, shown as a dashed loop. The wrapper then dispatches one lane, p01, on the integration checkout, which implements the sync version-skew advisory and the lockstep bump. A phase review sends the lane back once for a bounded fix round, another dashed loop. The lane then runs eight definition-of-done gates and two final review rounds, after which a configured exit gate blocks in its first generation and passes in a second generation on a different target. The wave PR is the remaining step.</desc>\n                <defs>\n                  <marker id=\"arrow\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\">\n                    <path class=\"arrow\" d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" />\n                  </marker>\n                  <marker id=\"arrow-muted\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\">\n                    <path class=\"arrow is-muted\" d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" />\n                  </marker>\n                </defs>\n                <g>\n                  <rect class=\"node\" x=\"330\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"52\" rx=\"8\" />\n                  <text class=\"node-label\" x=\"450\" y=\"40\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2026-08-19 execution program</text><text class=\"node-sub\" x=\"450\" y=\"57\" text-anchor=\"middle\">four waves, immutable</text>\n                  <rect class=\"node\" x=\"290\" y=\"112\" width=\"320\" height=\"52\" rx=\"8\" />\n                  <text class=\"node-label\" x=\"450\" y=\"136\" text-anchor=\"middle\">wave-2-execution</text><text class=\"node-sub\" x=\"450\" y=\"153\" text-anchor=\"middle\">wrapper OAT project, quick mode</text>\n                  <rect class=\"node\" x=\"24\" y=\"108\" width=\"210\" height=\"60\" rx=\"8\" />\n                  <text class=\"node-label\" x=\"129\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Plan gate</text><text class=\"node-sub\" x=\"129\" y=\"149\" text-anchor=\"middle\">configured artifact review</text>\n                  <text class=\"node-sub\" x=\"129\" y=\"160\" text-anchor=\"middle\">passed on round 3</text>\n                  <rect class=\"node is-lane\" x=\"190\" y=\"212\" width=\"520\" height=\"88\" rx=\"8\" />\n                  <text class=\"node-label\" x=\"450\" y=\"240\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Lane p01 — integration checkout</text><text class=\"node-sub\" x=\"450\" y=\"257\" text-anchor=\"middle\">external plan: warn-sync-version-skew</text>\n                  <text class=\"node-sub\" x=\"450\" y=\"274\" text-anchor=\"middle\">packages/cli/src/commands/sync + lockstep bump 0.2.34</text>\n                  <rect class=\"node\" x=\"290\" y=\"348\" width=\"320\" height=\"52\" rx=\"8\" />\n                  <text class=\"node-label\" x=\"450\" y=\"372\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Phase review p01</text><text class=\"node-sub\" x=\"450\" y=\"389\" text-anchor=\"middle\">two rounds, mutation battery</text>\n                  <rect class=\"node\" x=\"290\" y=\"436\" width=\"320\" height=\"52\" rx=\"8\" />\n                  <text class=\"node-label\" x=\"450\" y=\"460\" text-anchor=\"middle\">8 DoD gates + final review</text><text class=\"node-sub\" x=\"450\" y=\"477\" text-anchor=\"middle\">every exit code 0, two rounds</text>\n                  <rect class=\"node is-blocked\" x=\"90\" y=\"524\" width=\"290\" height=\"60\" rx=\"8\" />\n                  <text class=\"node-label\" x=\"235\" y=\"548\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Exit gate generation 1</text><text class=\"node-sub\" x=\"235\" y=\"565\" text-anchor=\"middle\">blocked: no artifact, 2 attempts</text>\n                  <rect class=\"node\" x=\"520\" y=\"524\" width=\"290\" height=\"60\" rx=\"8\" />\n                  <text class=\"node-label\" x=\"665\" y=\"548\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Exit gate generation 2</text><text class=\"node-sub\" x=\"665\" y=\"565\" text-anchor=\"middle\">passed on a cross-family target</text>\n                  <rect class=\"node is-goal\" x=\"330\" y=\"648\" width=\"240\" height=\"48\" rx=\"8\" />\n                  <text class=\"node-label\" x=\"450\" y=\"669\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Wave PR</text>\n                  <text class=\"node-sub\" x=\"450\" y=\"686\" text-anchor=\"middle\">remaining step</text>\n                </g>\n                <g>\n                  <path class=\"edge\" d=\"M450,68 V112\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\" />\n                  <path class=\"edge\" d=\"M290,128 H240\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\" />\n                  <path class=\"edge is-feedback\" d=\"M234,152 H284\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow-muted)\" />\n                  <path class=\"edge\" d=\"M450,164 V212\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\" />\n                  <path class=\"edge\" d=\"M450,300 V348\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\" />\n                  <path class=\"edge is-feedback\" d=\"M290,374 H60 V256 H184\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow-muted)\" />\n                  <path class=\"edge\" d=\"M450,400 V436\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\" />\n                  <path class=\"edge\" d=\"M450,488 V506 H235 V524\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\" />\n                  <path class=\"edge\" d=\"M450,488 V506 H665 V524\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\" />\n                  <path class=\"edge is-feedback\" d=\"M380,554 H514\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow-muted)\" />\n                  <path class=\"edge\" d=\"M665,584 V616 H450 V648\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\" />\n                </g>\n                <g>\n                  <text class=\"edge-label\" x=\"462\" y=\"94\">scopes the wave</text>\n                  <text class=\"edge-label\" x=\"246\" y=\"118\">wrapper plan</text>\n                  <text class=\"edge-label\" x=\"240\" y=\"180\">2 blocked rounds</text>\n                  <text class=\"edge-label\" x=\"462\" y=\"196\">one lane, no parallel group</text>\n                  <text class=\"edge-label\" x=\"462\" y=\"332\">reviewed at the task commit</text>\n                  <text class=\"edge-label\" x=\"78\" y=\"248\">fix round 1</text>\n                  <text class=\"edge-label\" x=\"462\" y=\"422\">after the review row passed</text>\n                  <text class=\"edge-label\" x=\"146\" y=\"514\">first target</text>\n                  <text class=\"edge-label\" x=\"682\" y=\"514\">second target</text>\n                  <text class=\"edge-label\" x=\"386\" y=\"546\">operator retarget</text>\n                  <text class=\"edge-label\" x=\"462\" y=\"640\">next</text>\n                </g>\n                <g>\n                  <path class=\"edge\" d=\"M24,704 H56\" />\n                  <text class=\"edge-label\" x=\"64\" y=\"708\">forward progress</text>\n                  <path class=\"edge is-feedback\" d=\"M200,704 H232\" />\n                  <text class=\"edge-label\" x=\"240\" y=\"708\">loop that fired</text>\n                </g>\n              </svg>\n            </div>\n            <figcaption>Flow of the wave. Solid edges are forward progress; dashed edges are the two loops that actually fired, the plan gate sending the wrapper plan back twice and the phase review sending the lane back once. The exit gate is the only place the wave left autonomy, and the wave PR is still ahead.</figcaption>\n          </figure>\n          <div class=\"lanes\">\n            <div class=\"lane\">\n              <h3>What the wrapper owns</h3>\n              <ul>\n                <li>Ordering, the drift-check addendum and the concurrency ceiling</li>\n                <li>The wrapper-level definition-of-done sequence and its captured exit codes</li>\n                <li>Review mapping, gate targets and dispatch policy</li>\n                <li>Commit scope naming, backlog archival and all bookkeeping</li>\n              </ul>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"lane is-secondary\">\n              <h3>What the external plan owns</h3>\n              <ul>\n                <li>Its drift check and STOP conditions</li>\n                <li>Its implementation steps and embedded verify gates</li>\n                <li>Its done criteria, review focus and test plan</li>\n                <li>The files it is allowed to write</li>\n              </ul>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n          <h3>Delivered surfaces</h3>\n          <div class=\"table-scroll\">\n            <table>\n              <caption>As-built boundaries</caption>\n              <thead>\n                <tr><th scope=\"col\">Surface</th><th scope=\"col\">Responsibility after the wave</th></tr>\n              </thead>\n              <tbody>\n                <tr>\n                  <th scope=\"row\"><code>sync/sync.types.ts</code></th>\n                  <td>Declares the per-scope diagnostic shape: the scope, the version that produced the manifest and the version now invoking sync.</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <th scope=\"row\"><code>sync/index.ts</code></th>\n                  <td>Derives the diagnostic at the single scope-plan construction site and emits one warning per skewed scope before the dry-run and apply branch, suppressed in JSON mode.</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <th scope=\"row\"><code>sync/apply.ts</code></th>\n                  <td>Restamps the manifest only when that same diagnostic is present, and reports the array in the apply envelope. No exit-code, count or eligibility expression changed.</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <th scope=\"row\"><code>sync/dry-run.ts</code></th>\n                  <td>Reports the same array in the dry-run envelope, including the no-op case where nothing would be applied.</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <th scope=\"row\">Public package manifests</th>\n                  <td>Five packages plus the generated version asset, all at 0.2.34.</td>\n                </tr>\n              </tbody>\n            </table>\n          </div>\n          <p class=\"note\">The manifest schema, the manifest loader and the absent-or-invalid manifest semantics were deliberately left untouched; only the loader's test file gained a case.</p>\n        </section>\n        <section id=\"implementation-record\" aria-labelledby=\"implementation-record-heading\">\n          <h2 id=\"implementation-record-heading\">What changed</h2>\n          <p>The lane landed as one task commit plus one append-only fix commit, so every SHA a review cites still resolves. The task commit touched twelve files; the fix round touched three.</p>\n          <div class=\"table-scroll\">\n            <table>\n              <caption>Implementation record</caption>\n              <thead>\n                <tr><th scope=\"col\">Component</th><th scope=\"col\">Notable change</th><th scope=\"col\">Commits</th></tr>\n              </thead>\n              <tbody>\n                <tr>\n                  <th scope=\"row\">Skew diagnostic</th>\n                  <td>Each scope plan carries an optional diagnostic derived while the plan is built: the scope name, the version recorded in the loaded manifest and the version invoking sync. It is present only when the two differ.</td>\n                  <td class=\"evidence\">b257e908</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <th scope=\"row\">Warning placement</th>\n                  <td>One warning per skewed scope is logged before the branch into dry-run or apply, which is before the only route to saving a manifest. JSON mode returns early instead of writing text.</td>\n                  <td class=\"evidence\">b257e908</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <th scope=\"row\">JSON envelopes</th>\n                  <td>Both the apply and the dry-run envelope expose the array unconditionally, empty when nothing is skewed, including the dry-run case where no operation is planned.</td>\n                  <td class=\"evidence\">b257e908</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <th scope=\"row\">Restamp coupling</th>\n                  <td>Apply stopped carrying its own copy of the comparison and now derives the restamp from the diagnostic. The duplicate predicate, its unused import and two unreachable empty-string guards were removed together.</td>\n                  <td class=\"evidence\">023c2229</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <th scope=\"row\">Lockstep bump</th>\n                  <td>Five public package manifests and the generated version asset moved from 0.2.33 to 0.2.34. The lockfile records workspace links, so it was correctly left unchanged.</td>\n                  <td class=\"evidence\">b257e908</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <th scope=\"row\">Closeout bookkeeping</th>\n                  <td>Orchestration synthesis, the summary roll-up and backlog archival for the tracked item, plus the two review receives and the exit-gate generations.</td>\n                  <td class=\"evidence\">acc0c292, a4a7804d, 2e106b66</td>\n                </tr>\n              </tbody>\n            </table>\n          </div>\n          <p class=\"note\">One file outside the source plan's declared scope was written, the manifest loader's test file, and it was declared up front because the plan's own test plan authorises it.</p>\n        </section>\n        <section id=\"validation-evidence\" aria-labelledby=\"validation-evidence-heading\">\n          <h2 id=\"validation-evidence-heading\">How it was checked</h2>\n          <p>An advisory that fires after the thing it warns about is worthless, so most of the evidence here is about ordering and about the two places where the advisory could silently stop agreeing with the behaviour it describes.</p>\n          <div class=\"table-scroll\">\n            <table>\n              <caption>Validation evidence</caption>\n              <thead>\n                <tr><th scope=\"col\">Check</th><th scope=\"col\">Where it ran</th><th scope=\"col\">Observed result</th><th scope=\"col\">Limits</th></tr>\n              </thead>\n              <tbody>\n                <tr>\n                  <th scope=\"row\">Focused suites</th>\n                  <td>Sync command and manifest loader suites, at the fix commit</td>\n                  <td class=\"ok\">55 tests pass, up from 41 at the wave base.</td>\n                  <td class=\"note\">The manifest loader itself is unmodified; it gained one structural case.</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <th scope=\"row\">Ordering probe</th>\n                  <td>Phase review, destructive probe with the manifest directory made unwritable</td>\n                  <td class=\"ok\">The warning reaches standard error, then the restamp fails hard and the manifest is unchanged.</td>\n                  <td class=\"note\">Proves ordering by observation rather than by reading the call sequence.</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <th scope=\"row\">Mutation battery</th>\n                  <td>Phase review rounds 1 and 2, reviewer-designed mutations</td>\n                  <td class=\"ok\">Reorder, delete, JSON-field delete and predicate desync all turn tests red. The desync case is caught only by the coupling test the fix round added.</td>\n                  <td class=\"note\">Not part of the committed suite; the mutations were applied to scratch copies.</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <th scope=\"row\">End-to-end probes</th>\n                  <td>Final review, nine probes against the built CLI</td>\n                  <td class=\"ok\">JSON mode emits pure parseable output with zero bytes on standard error; equal, older, newer, absent and invalid manifests each behave as specified.</td>\n                  <td class=\"note\">Probe scratch lived outside the worktree and was removed.</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <th scope=\"row\">Definition of done</th>\n                  <td>Wave branch, 8 gates captured individually</td>\n                  <td class=\"ok\">Every exit code 0: check, type-check, test, build, skill-bump check, release version check, release validation and docs build.</td>\n                  <td class=\"note\">The release version check needs a current upstream ref, so a fetch precedes every run.</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <th scope=\"row\">Cross-model review</th>\n                  <td>Codex on the uncommitted diff, twice</td>\n                  <td class=\"ok\">Zero findings both times.</td>\n                  <td class=\"note\">Independent of the same-model phase reviewer, which did find a medium.</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <th scope=\"row\">Reviews</th>\n                  <td>Plan gate 3 rounds, phase 2 rounds, final 2 rounds, plus the configured exit gate</td>\n                  <td class=\"ok\">Every row passed. The exit gate re-ran the whole definition of done in the foreground and reported no critical or important findings.</td>\n                  <td class=\"note\">Two minor findings were re-verified and deliberately deferred rather than closed.</td>\n                </tr>\n              </tbody>\n            </table>\n          </div>\n          <p class=\"note\">The finding that mattered was not a bug in the shipped behaviour. It was the duplicated comparison: correct on the day, and free to drift on any later day. The fix removed the duplicate rather than testing it.</p>\n        </section>\n        <section id=\"outcome\" aria-labelledby=\"outcome-heading\">\n          <h2 id=\"outcome-heading\">Where this leaves the repository</h2>\n          <div class=\"outcome\">\n            <div class=\"works\">\n              <h3><span class=\"label\">Works now</span></h3>\n              <ul>\n                <li>A stale sync manifest announces itself once per affected scope before apply overwrites the evidence, naming both the producing and the invoking version.</li>\n                <li>Machine consumers read the same facts from a structured array present in both the apply and the dry-run envelope, with human text still suppressed in JSON mode.</li>\n                <li>The restamp and the advisory are one decision rather than two agreeing copies, held in place by a coupling test.</li>\n                <li>The five public packages sit at 0.2.34 and the tracked backlog item for this defect is closed.</li>\n              </ul>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"gaps\">\n              <h3><span class=\"label\">Did not ship</span></h3>\n              <ul>\n                <li>Skew is still only advisory. No exit code, count, eligibility rule or manifest schema changed, exactly as the source plan required.</li>\n                <li>Three sibling commands still restamp the recorded version silently. That was ruled outside the plan's scope and filed as a backlog candidate.</li>\n                <li>A deferred minor: the field the restamp now keys off is optional on its type, so a hand-built plan object that omits it would type-check and skip the restamp. Unreachable through the real construction path.</li>\n                <li>The wave PR has not been opened or merged; the recorded closeout stops at the completed pre-approval steps.</li>\n              </ul>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"next\">\n              <h3><span class=\"label\">For the next reader</span></h3>\n              <ul>\n                <li>The next edit to the sync plan types should make that diagnostic field non-optional; that is the recorded trigger for the deferred minor.</li>\n                <li>Take the three sibling restamp sites together with the \"no changes required\" message that a restamp-only apply still prints.</li>\n                <li>Generate the project summary before archiving a backlog item, not after; this wave got that order wrong and recorded it as a deviation for the remaining waves.</li>\n                <li>When a configured gate blocks at its attempt cap, that is an operator boundary. Changing the target is a decision, not a retry.</li>\n              </ul>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </section>\n        <footer>\n          <p>Recap built from the approved lifecycle artifacts of the OAT project <code>.oat/projects/shared/wave-2-execution</code>: <code>plan.md</code>, <code>implementation.md</code> and <code>summary.md</code>. Commit references are short SHAs on the <code>wave-2-execution</code> branch. Line and file pointers quoted in those artifacts shift with later edits and should be verified against HEAD.</p>\n        </footer>\n      </main>\n    </div>\n<script>\n      (() => {\n        const links = [...document.querySelectorAll('.toc a[href^=\"#\"]')];\n        const targets = links\n          .map((link) => document.querySelector(link.getAttribute('href')))\n          .filter(Boolean);\n        const observer = new IntersectionObserver(\n          (entries) => {\n            for (const entry of entries) {\n              if (!entry.isIntersecting) continue;\n              links.forEach((link) =>\n                link.classList.toggle(\n                  'active',\n                  link.getAttribute('href') === `#${entry.target.id}`,\n                ),\n              );\n            }\n          },\n          { rootMargin: '-15% 0px -70% 0px' },\n        );\n        targets.forEach((target) => observer.observe(target));\n      })();\n    </script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
